From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:21:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 385/638] [AROS] Bridge Viz canvas presents across Processes

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model

AI_STATUS: build-validated, runtime-pending

ROOT_CAUSE: With --single-process removed, Viz owns a separately relocated ArosWindowManager whose process-local widget map cannot resolve the browser Process's native Intuition window. Raster frames reached PresentCanvas but every presentation returned false.

FIX_REASON: Publish a browser-owned Exec MsgPort and synchronously forward plain canvas metadata from Viz. AROS's shared address space lets the browser paint the same pixel buffer without a copy; ReplyMsg keeps the buffer alive until presentation finishes.

SCOPE: AROS Ozone window manager only. No loader, relocation, GOT, PIC, GPU, or non-AROS behavior changes.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-v8-library -j32 chrome passed 6/6; resulting chrome remains AROS ELF64 ET_REL with a zero-size .got section.

RISK: The first bridge uses one public presentation-port name, so concurrent independent Chromium browser instances require a later per-instance rendezvous token.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: runtime 25 multiprocess present-failure evidence
